<title>UK: EBRD appoints exec to oversee banking operations.</title>
<headline>EBRD appoints exec to oversee banking operations.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD) has appointed Charles Frank as first vice president to oversee its banking operations, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>Frank, who is expected to begin on September 1, will suceed Ron Freeman who will leave the bank this month, the EBRD said.</p>
<p>In his new role, Frank also will provide strategic and management input into the bank's operations and will chair the credit committee which reviews all projects before consideration by the EBRD's Board of Directors.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, 44 171 542 5110</p>
